6.123.m:
Kārttikeya said:
O Lord, I wish to hear the supreme vow among vows:
the rule of fasting for a month, and its result as spoken [in scripture];

6.125.m:
Vasiṣṭha said:
Formerly, O king, for twelve years the cloud did not rain;
troubled and emaciated by that, the subjects scattered to all ten directions.
